    {
      "text": "folder 90 - 009\nWell, unintentionally, I proved the point I made in my Metz speech. I remembered a discarded alternative track, that depicted in TEARS. When I saw \"Acts\" in 2-74 I was seeing an alternate present; this is why the two \"spatiotemporal sets\" blended together syntonically. I was seeing the alternate present I had written about; this alternate present, this dystopia, was one massive zero. As I said supra, my anamnesis was not of the past but of the present, of a rejected choic",
      "matched_alias": "Tagomi",
      "term_id": "TERM_tagomi",
      "term_name": "Tagomi",
      "term_slug": "tagomi"
    },
    {
      "text": "Last edit about 2 months ago by Gabriel Mckee\nfolder 90 - 008\n\nfolder 90 - 008\nwhy, but this was the anamnesis) a discarded zero branch of the forking, that this forking, this zero choice and rejection, then a shift to the one or on fork instead -- this goes on constantly but we don't remember it. I remembered it. Anamnesis is, then, the key. Had I not experienced anamnesis before the arrival of the Xerox missive I would not have been aware (1) that the Xerox missive was coming; (2) exact",
